# Project: [Full-Stack App]
Frontend: React + TypeScript (src/client/)
Backend: Express + TypeScript (src/server/)
Database: PostgreSQL + Prisma (prisma/)

## Conventions
- Frontend: functional components, hooks only, no class components
- Backend: route -> service -> database layer separation
- Shared types in src/shared/types.ts
- All database access through Prisma (no raw SQL)
- API responses use { data, error, meta } shape

## Structure
- src/client/ (React frontend)
- src/server/routes/ (API routes)
- src/server/services/ (business logic)
- src/shared/ (shared types and utilities)
- prisma/ (schema and migrations)
- tests/ (mirrors src/ structure)

## Rules
- Never modify prisma/migrations/ files
- Never modify .env files
- Frontend changes must not break backend tests
- Backend changes must not break frontend types
- Run full test suite before committing

## Workflow
- Show plan before cross-boundary changes (client + server)
- Use shared types for API contracts
